nt-family:Helvetica\"> where they stay. Will they </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">found</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> new human supporters? Or will they be hunted by the mortals or their own kind?</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Family matters</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> \u2013 With colonists, come to the America totally new mix of Beasts and their Horrors. Not all of them recognize one another as Family. Understanding that all Beasts are Children of the same Dark Mother maybe difficult. PCs are thrown between two communities of Begotten, that cannot understand one another, like European and First Nations Beasts.</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> It's on PCs shoulders to </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">to</span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> communicate between two sides \u2013 or the war will ensure.</span></span></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-28-2018, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T00:09:23-08:00","id":1190166,"title":"","content":"Seeds for next Era...<br /> <b><u>Tyrants of the Rising Sun (Occupied Japan, 1945-1952)</u></b><br /> In August 1945, the world and the Primordial Dream was changed forever. The atomic bombs dropped on Hiroshima and Nagasaki, and the world was introduced to a brand new fear that would dominate the rest of the century: the fear of nuclear annihilation. That weapons technology had reached a point where tens of thousands of people could die in an instant. The people of Japan know this better then anything else. Especially since the radiation still lingers on in the sites where the bombs dropped. This is further exacerbated when American forces occupied Japan for half a decade, increasing anxiety and lethargy on losing in a major world war. The combination of new and old fears would create...an unusual effect on the Horrors created in this time. Years later the Japanese Begotten still wasn't sure what it was, but the Horrors all grew to enormous size, almost as tall as buildings. Whatever they were, a new kind of Beast was created in the embers of the dying Empire of the Rising Sun: kaiju. From oversized insects, to mutated lizards and dinosaurs, to sea dragons that crawl on land, Japan is about to face a new kind of fear.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Chronicles Seeds:</b></span></span></span></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>D</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>aikaij\u016b</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">\u2013</span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Atomic blasts in </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Hiroshima and Nagasaki</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">born new Fears in humanity \u2013 fear of nuclear annihilation. </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Theories of mutated, giant monsters capture </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Japanese</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> imagination and dreams. </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">In coming weeks there is strange phenomena on Begotten \u2013 all newly Devoured have </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>Looming Presence</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Atavisms from their great new Horrors, regardless of their Family.</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Begotten are given this powers on top of normal two Atavisms they come from their transformation. Those new Beasts have also intrinsic pull to be Apex in their local communities, to overthrown previous ones. </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">( I</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> think about special Condition</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> here</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">. )</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Coming Begotten ar</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">e compelled to join their own Broods and in groups fight for supremacy on Primordial Dream of Japan</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> - and in the end fight inside the Brood to shown the last, most </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">powerful</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Apex, once and for all.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>New Merit</b></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>: Kaiju (****)</b></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Prerequisite: </b></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>Loomin</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>g</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i> Presence</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Atavism</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Horror of this Begotten is </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">extremely</span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> imposing. The effective Size bonus by using </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>Looming </i></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>Presence</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> is twice normal \u2013 so Normal Effect </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">gives Beast Size bonus of Lair x 2 and Satiety </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Expenditure</span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> makes Size bonus of Lair x 4. Ture Apex of Kaiju kind can rise up to effective Size 45 and more!</span></span></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>\u200bEnemy W</b></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>ithin</b></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> \u2013 American forces are </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">occupying</span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> previous </span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Empire of the Rising Sun</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">. Many traditional Japanese \u2013 and Japan's Beasts \u2013 are feeling betrayed or that they will lost their way with U.S. Military. Some islands Begotten are using their powers to solve the problems of their human kin, not other Children of Dark Mother. There </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">are</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> attacks on humans \u2013 more </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">gruesome</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> than normal Hunger feeding \u2013 and some Edo-styled markings, </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">praising</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> 'original' Japan's culture. There is </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">resurgence</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> in classical Japan's myths Horrors and there is rise of 'pure' feeding of Hungers. Will PCs uncover orthodox faction in Begotten society? Will they stop them, when their Lesson Teaching will become </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">massacring American civilians?</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Manga </b></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">\u2013</span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Manga as ar</span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">t style has roots i</span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">n </span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">U</span></span><a href=\"https://pl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ukiyo-e\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">kiyo-e</span></span></a><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">, traditional style of Edo period. </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">These pieces</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> were heavily </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">influenced</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> by American comics and animation \u2013 mainly Disney works \u2013 and Manga evolved by </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">intermingling</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> of those two directions. Creation of this mix has interesting \u2013 and somehow </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">terrifying</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> - effect on Primordial Dream. It created being similar to Horror but less imposing on first sight. Avatar of Manga idea is hunting for Begotten \u2013 both Japan and American - </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">and when </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">finding</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> one, she </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">joins</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> second Horror </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">for looking of new 'art'. Those Manga-Spawn are highly unstable, with weird and unstable Hungers.</span></span></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-28-2018, 10:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T05:16:39-08:00","id":1190207,"title":"","content":"I really like the era ideas you guys came up with. I gotta admit the Cath Maige Tuired courtesy of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> sounds very cool... fits perfectly with the &quot;Myths and Legends&quot; theme of Beast.<br /> The Wendigo one also is very appealing to me, but my favourite so far (which totally surprised me) is <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a>' The Cold, Icy Ocean. Something about meshing Titanic, Makara and a scavenger hunt is weirdly intriguing to me, despite this being an Era I am generally not much interested in.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> I... don't really see where your problem was? After all, you came up with <i>several </i>chronicle seeds for just one Era in a span of 2 hours (assuming you did other stuff during that time, too), so obviously the Era write-ups were easily enough for you to come up with an idea. I also never asked for explicit chronicle seeds, just having an Era outline is often enough to spawn hundreds of them for me and, I am certain, others - you included (see above statement). Not that I am against specific seeds, but in general, the idea was to gather possible fun Eras to set a chronicle in. That seems to have worked quite well imo.<br /> The perceived 'lack of a focus' doesn't really cut it as an argument for me, or rather I don't understand what you mean by that: If you go with &quot;hunt&quot; for Werewolves, it'd be &quot;Feed and teach lessons&quot; for Beasts. I don't see why that is not as good a focus or &quot;a general problem with BtP&quot;.<br /> Beast is more sandbox than some other gamelines, true, but you can<br /> - hunt for prey to Feed<br /> - try to become the Apex<br /> - try to stay ahead of Heroes<br /> - go for an Inheritance<br /> - look for the Dark Mother<br /> or participate in any other gameline's favourite shenanigans.<br /> To a degree, Beast is, just as any other gameline, about finding your place in a new world, striking a balance between two sides of yourself. It is about getting control of your own life's narrative (which here happens to be an actual force). (The latter would fit perfectly with Japan after WW2 in numerous ways, come to think of it.)<br /> And finally, a main theme of Beast is Family - making and breaking relationships makes for a very fine focus, as far as I am concerned, and should allow for stories just as interesting as searching for the latest MacGuffin, if not more so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 02-28-2018, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T05:29:55-08:00","id":1190214,"title":"","content":"I'm toying with the idea of a Dark Era focused on the birth of the psychoanalysis. Freud, Jung, dreams, science, mental health and legends. I might consider writing that once Geist comes out and I complete the one I'm doing now, since it would be a nice period to explore through Beast's perspective and a whole different kind of Era compared to the one I've written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T07:51:00-08:00","id":1190270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1189434-begotten-of-the-past?p=1190207#post1190207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wendigo one also is very appealing to me, but my favourite so far (which totally surprised me) is <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a>' The Cold, Icy Ocean. Something about meshing Titanic, Makara and a scavenger hunt is weirdly intriguing to me, despite this being an Era I am generally not much interested in.</div> </div> </div> </div>That feels pretty awesome! Thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T08:05:13-08:00","id":1190274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1189434-begotten-of-the-past?p=1190207#post1190207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The perceived 'lack of a focus' doesn't really cut it as an argument for me, or rather I don't understand what you mean by that: If you go with &quot;hunt&quot; for Werewolves, it'd be &quot;Feed and teach lessons&quot; for Beasts. I don't see why that is not as good a focus or &quot;a general problem with BtP&quot;.<br /> Beast is more sandbox than some other gamelines, true, but you can<br /> - hunt for prey to Feed<br /> - try to become the Apex<br /> - try to stay ahead of Heroes<br /> - go for an Inheritance<br /> - look for the Dark Mother<br /> or participate in any other gameline's favourite shenanigans.<br /> To a degree, Beast is, just as any other gameline, about finding your place in a new world, striking a balance between two sides of yourself. It is about getting control of your own life's narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>You see, it's a problem with <b>Beast: The Primodial</b> me and few other STs I talked to have. It's all about 'my Beast', not the group at large - ironically to Family theme of the game. Werewolves hunt together in packs. Mages uncover mystical secret in cabals. Even vampires are doing their politics by pulling coteries resources together. In <b>Beast</b> you sate YOUR OWN Hunger. YOU are aiming to become Apex. Go YOURSELF for Inheritance. All those actions are done by ONE PC, not whole group. <b>BtP</b>, like <b>Promethean the Created</b>, seems to be made for solo games - the 'snowflake issue' - and this is problem for many STs wanting to run it as multi-players group. It's a MUCH less problem than <b>PtC</b> - but it's there. So this is why I need Chronicles Seeds - to see <i>possibility</i> for chronicle for few PCs as one story in <b>BtP</b> - not collection of solo games mixed together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-28-2018, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T08:50:49-08:00","id":1190291,"title":"","content":"Aknowledging each other's needs, goals and identity as individuals while trying to find a common ground in order to live together and grow is a thing Familes do, though.<br /> <br /> Or should but don't, which is another source of story hooks and character interactions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-28-2018, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T09:46:04-08:00","id":1190313,"title":"","content":"Added Chronicles Seeds for the post WW2 Japan Era...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1189434-begotten-of-the-past?p=1190166#post1190166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Chronicles Seeds:</b></span></span></span><br /> </span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>D</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>aikaij\u016b</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">\u2013</span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Atomic blasts in </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Hiroshima and Nagasaki</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">born new Fears in humanity \u2013 fear of nuclear annihilation. </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Theories of mutated, giant monsters capture </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Japanese</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> imagination and dreams. </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">In coming weeks there is strange phenomena on Begotten \u2013 all newly Devoured have </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>Looming Presence</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Atavisms from their great new Horrors, regardless of their Family.</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Begotten are given this powers on top of normal two Atavisms they come from their transformation. Those new Beasts have also intrinsic pull to be Apex in their local communities, to overthrown previous ones. </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">( I</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> think about special Condition</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> here</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">. )</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Coming Begotten ar</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">e compelled to join their own Broods and in groups fight for supremacy on Primordial Dream of Japan</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> - and in the end fight inside the Brood to shown the last, most </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">powerful</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Apex, once and for all.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>New Merit</b></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>: Kaiju (***)</b></span></span><br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Prerequisite: </b></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>Loomin</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>g</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i> Presence</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Atavism</span></span><br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Horror of this Begotten is </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">extremely</span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> imposing. The effective Size bonus by using </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>Looming </i></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>Presence</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> is twice normal \u2013 so Normal Effect </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">gives Beast Size bonus of Lair x 2 and Satiety </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Expenditure</span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> makes Size bonus of Lair x 4. Ture Apex of Kaiju kind can rise up to effective Size 45 and more!</span></span><br /> </span></span></span><br /> <ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>\u200bEnemy W</b></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>ithin</b></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> \u2013 American forces are </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">occupying</span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> previous </span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Empire of the Rising Sun</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">. Many traditional Japanese \u2013 and Japan's Beasts \u2013 are feeling betrayed or that they will lost their way with U.S. Military. Some islands Begotten are using their powers to solve the problems of their human kin, not other Children of Dark Mother. There </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">are</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> attacks on humans \u2013 more </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">gruesome</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> than normal Hunger feeding \u2013 and some Edo-styled markings, </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">praising</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> 'original' Japan's culture. There is </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">resurgence</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> in classical Japan's myths Horrors and there is rise of 'pure' feeding of Hungers. Will PCs uncover orthodox faction in Begotten society? Will they stop them, when their Lesson Teaching will become </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">massacring American civilians?</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Manga </b></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">\u2013</span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Manga as ar</span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">t style has roots i</span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">n </span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">U</span></span><a href=\"https://pl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ukiyo-e\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">kiyo-e</span></span></a><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">, traditional style of Edo period. </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">These pieces</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> were heavily </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">influenced</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> by American comics and animation \u2013 mainly Disney works \u2013 and Manga evolved by </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">intermingling</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> of those two directions. Creation of this mix has interesting \u2013 and somehow </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">terrifying</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> - effect on Primordial Dream. It created being similar to Horror but less imposing on first sight. Avatar of Manga idea is hunting for Begotten \u2013 both Japan and American - </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">and when </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">finding</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> one, she </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">joins</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> second Horror </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">for looking of new 'art'. Those Manga-Spawn are highly unstable, with weird and unstable Hungers.</span></span></li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T10:52:31-08:00","id":1190337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1189434-begotten-of-the-past?p=1190274#post1190274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You see, it's a problem with <b>Beast: The Primodial</b> me and few other STs I talked to have. It's all about 'my Beast', not the group at large - ironically to Family theme of the game. Werewolves hunt together in packs. Mages uncover mystical secret in cabals. Even vampires are doing their politics by pulling coteries resources together. In <b>Beast</b> you sate YOUR OWN Hunger. YOU are aiming to become Apex. Go YOURSELF for Inheritance. All those actions are done by ONE PC, not whole group. <b>BtP</b>, like <b>Promethean the Created</b>, seems to be made for solo games - the 'snowflake issue' - and this is problem for many STs wanting to run it as multi-players group. It's a MUCH less problem than <b>PtC</b> - but it's there. So this is why I need Chronicles Seeds - to see <i>possibility</i> for chronicle for few PCs as one story in <b>BtP</b> - not collection of solo games mixed together.</div> </div> </div> </div>I grant you that Werewolves have a very special bond as a Pack In-Setting. But Mages uncover mystical secrets in Cabals because they cannot do it by themselves, or a majority (In-setting) would. Coteries, likewise, break apart once they don't need each other anymore. Demon Rings (?) are more of an uneasy truce than anything else. Changelings and Hunters at least share similar traumata, but the idea of &quot;you have come together as people who went through the same supernatural event&quot; is the basic premise of the whole gig.<br /> A special bond that is shared by the members <i>beyond </i>that basic premise IMO only applies to Werewolf, Promethean and Beast. As a Werewolf player, I don't need to tell you about werewolves. Prometheans are united by a common goal, the desire to keep each other in check and on the right path, mitigate inherent drawbacks of their existance and <i>metaphysically bind themselves to each other</i>. Beasts see below.<br /> Regarding the 'Sate YOUR HUNGER': same is true for every other splat. Vampires sate their hunger, not their friends'. You cannot eat for a friend. Even the 'hunting as a Pack' thing is a desire of singular werewolves.<br /> <br /> I don't think Beast is made for Solo-Adventures (nor do I think Promethean is) - they work solo, yes, but so do most splats. However, they <i>shine </i>with a small group. Also, &quot;Snowflaking&quot; is more of a problem with Z-Splats etc, when people need to be &quot;the only/first/last of their kind&quot;, feel the need to be more rare and powerful/useful/special than their fellow players or otherwise cannot be satisfied with a 'normal' template to breath life into. Beasts are merely quite customizable (though, at least mechanically, not to the same degree as Changelings and Demons). Not bashing z-splats here - I love them, they can add a great layer of meaning or depth to a character, but shouldn't completely define the character.<br /> Futhermore, the moment you play a one-person-game, (and as I said, that works JUST as well with every other splat as it does with Beast, with the possible exception of W:tF, imo) everything becomes 'Special Snowflake-y' very quickly (unless you specifically grognard it VtM style): Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Changeling, Demon, Beast, Mummy, Hunter, Geist - doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> Some more points on Beasts being about &quot;My Beast&quot;:<br /> - One way of sating a Beast's Hunger is, literally, to help their Family members feed themselves (help Mages hunt for Artifacts, participate in a Siskur-Dah, help a Changeling get that Glamour...). This comes especially in handy for those Beasts that take issue with their Horror's Hunger. That is plenty of incentive to not work alone, and even go out of your way to help others. There is even similarity to how Uratha accept other Supernaturals if they help them Hunt - there is a purpose to the action, and usually mutually beneficial.<br /> - One major way of expanding their Lair (a.k.a. grow as a Monster/person) is to seek out places where your supernatural relatives left a lasting impression. The more the Beast learns about what took place, the more people and supernaturals involved they meet, the better their chances of finding and claiming a chamber. This is a very strong incentive to learn more about the occult history of the area, get to know the local things that go bump in the night (not just splats, but also horrors, classic antagonists, ghosts, spirits, whatever - the more you get to know, the better!). This is even mechanically encouraged by giving the same amount of dice for being the supernatural that caused the impact in question and having encountered the supernatural in question (+3). Even more dice are given if the Beast has Family Ties with this supernatural being (+5!).<br /> - Broodmates can draw on each other's Lair Traits to call down their own - literally exponentially making them stronger than lone wolves; a very literal &quot;Power of Friendship&quot;. The Mother's Kiss even underlines this by giving Beasts a Mentor-Stance - the more powerful a Beast, the better it can support WEAKER Family members. This makes the most sense if both have a different focus and thus compliment each other. Furthermore, being strongly acquainted with certain splat grants you access to new powers: Nightmares are literally reflections of how other supernaturals (or even specific individuals) spread Fear - a Beast looking to increase its toolset needs to interact meaningfully with other supernaturals.<br /> - Like all the other splats, Beasts have unique antagonists trying to hunt them down - unlike in most other cases, though, their enemies get special powers that only work against the Children - plenty of incentive to try and invite other supernaturals into their Brood, to better defend themselves.<br /> - &quot;Go YOURSELF for Inheritance&quot;. Well, first of all 2 out of 3 Inheritances are more like alternate game-overs/suicides than winning. Next, a Beast going for an Inheritance is very similar to a Mage going for Archmage. That is also one Mage going for it, not a whole Cabal having the goal of making that one dude Archmage. And if you say &quot;well, they can support him and he relies on them&quot; - well, duh, <i>same for Broods</i>.<br /> - Beasts get nice little set-ups to pretend to be part of another splat. This is to encourage IC exploration of other supernatural societies. Plenty of story-hooks here: Beast new in town, follows the first vamp into their society, becomes friends and boom, fudges up and their cover is blown. How will their alleged 'friends' react? Or: Beast went undercover in a Cabal for some time, but cannot keep lying to their Family any longer. But they might decide it makes a more interesting test subject than friend, or consider it a threat. On the other hand, they might welcome the options the Beast brings to the table. But then how will others react to them indulging a 'pet'? etc etc.<br /> - Not every Beast wants to be Apex, same as not every Kindred wants to be Prince. It's<i> An</i> endgame, not the only one. Plus Broods might like to have the Apex in their Brood, because it would give THEM ALL quite the substantial powerboost (one of our Lair Traits is in EVERY Chamber? AWESOME! LET'S DO IT!). So they might actually work together to make one amongst them Apex.<br /> - Core literally states that most Beasts have an inherent desire for companionship and do not want to be left to their own devices. That isn't too tough to roleplay, imo.<br /> - Beasts need to act physically, but also mentally and socially. They have the same needs as all other splats to cover the Heroic Groups basis (Be that Tank, Brawler, Smart Guy, Silver Tongue, Thief or whatever other template you want to use).<br /> And, most importantly imo for non-mechanical reasons:<br /> - Broods <i>literally </i>connect their 'Souls' and can take a hike in each other's soul. They even invite their Cousin Broodmates into their 'Souls'. You think this sort of connection will be as haphazard and instable as most Coteries? On the other hand, you doubt it would be as strong as a Promethean Branded Throng or Werewolf Pack?<br /> <br /> Honestly, the things you mentioned don't make sense to me. You see lack of focus; I see wealth of opportunities. You see &quot;Hunting together&quot; in Werewolf, but don't see &quot;Family&quot; in Beast?<br /> The way I see it, a Werewolf grows strong alone, to work primarily as part of a Pack - a Beast might (<i>might!</i> not does!) work alone, but mostly grows <i>thanks to others</i>.<br /> I don't see how that is, at all, problematic. Different, sure. It's supposed to be, it's a different gameline.<br /> Maybe it's just not your cup of tea.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> The Kaiju Merit is seriously powerful and should probably cost 4 dots. A Lair 3 Beast without Giant and 2 Stamina could spend a Satiety to gain 6 HP and run around with 19 HP. That is seriously tanky even on it's own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 02-28-2018, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T13:28:50-08:00","id":1190405,"title":"","content":"If I were to do a post WW2 Japan Era that plays with Kaiju (great idea, by the way) I'd personally explore that element another way. Got no issue with giant Horrors as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4418_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4418\" data-vbnamecard=\"4418\">tasti man LH</a> proposed them, it mirrors the fears of the age and it's absolutely fitting both in an in-setting and meta way, but if I decide to also have more physical Kaiju with a direct mechanical impact, I'd treat them as a condition rather than a Merit. Not a desiderable one, mind you: your Horror grows and pushes from the ephemeral into the material making you lose control of your body and mind. Can it be reversed and fought back? Why is it happening to some Begotten while others seem immune? Who knows, but when a Beast succumbs to it rampage and destruction ensue.<br /> <br /> It shifts it from being a boon into a panic-inducing curse, but plays well with the themes of Beast and the Era. Might even try to make it fit into the current state of Tokyo according to the core.<br /> <br /> That said, that Era is not an idea of mine and I'm not telling anyone how to do that. Just throwing out my two cents.<br /> <br /> Side note: post WW2 Japan was not just Kaiju movies and there's plenty more to explore, but this reminds me about vague idea I had was about a Era related to classic monster movies. Universal Monsters, sci-fi from the fifties and movies like Blob or The Beast From 20.000 Fathoms. It's a little silly, self-aware and not as dramatic as others, but it's also about a time were the whole Family found a place in medias and common imaginary. But yes, it would require some work and focus in order to function properly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-28-2018, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T13:41:18-08:00","id":1190410,"title":"","content":"And think of everyone who has a bone to pick with Japan after WW2, thanks to all the abuse (read; atrocities where comparing them to the Nazis is not hyperbole) they heaped on other countries. You\u2019d think some individually powerful supernaturals with ties to their nation would come to Japan to terrorize the finally-broken populace. Alternatively, the Japanese rule having inspired Horrors in the form of various y\u014dkai around Asia, with Beasts manifesting their oppressors\u2019 culture on a literal soul-deep level that won\u2019t sit well with other Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T13:44:04-08:00","id":1190412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1189434-begotten-of-the-past?p=1190410#post1190410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And think of everyone who has a bone to pick with Japan after WW2, thanks to all the abuse (read; atrocities where comparing them to the Nazis is not hyperbole) they heaped on other countries. You\u2019d think some individually powerful supernaturals with ties to their nation would come to Japan to terrorize the finally-broken populace. Alternatively, the Japanese rule having inspired Horrors in the form of various y\u014dkai around Asia, with Beasts manifesting their oppressors\u2019 culture on a literal soul-deep level that won\u2019t sit well with other Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>The destruction of the Imperial paradigm would likely have repercussions, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T13:49:32-08:00","id":1190414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1189434-begotten-of-the-past?p=1190412#post1190412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The destruction of the Imperial paradigm would likely have repercussions, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Old gods of traditional/local Shinto and the conquered territories manifesting as Beasts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T13:56:17-08:00","id":1190418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1189434-begotten-of-the-past?p=1190405#post1190405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd treat them as a condition rather than a Merit. Not a desiderable one, mind you: your Horror grows and pushes from the ephemeral into the material making you lose control of your body and mind. Can it be reversed and fought back? Why is it happening to some Begotten while others seem immune? Who knows, but when a Beast succumbs to it rampage and destruction ensue.</div> </div> </div> </div>So something like an undesired Merger taking place? Or more of a &quot;I had Amnesia and in the meantime the inner Monster took over and destroyed everything&quot; kinda deal?<br /> Kinda have to think of it like a Countdown: &quot;Bad news, boy. You got x days, if the conditions are not met, your Horror drives itself into your body and everything that you are or were as a human being disappears to make room for a Gojira running amok. What are the conditions? Pff, fuck if I know.&quot;<br /> Plus maybe losing access to some basic Beast abilities like the instant-positive impression. After all, Kaiju duke it out and except for some team ups are more of a free-for-all-mindset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T13:57:14-08:00","id":1190419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1189434-begotten-of-the-past?p=1190414#post1190414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Old gods of traditional/local Shinto and the conquered territories manifesting as Beasts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. Also Horrors resembling ghosts of old things - dressed in imperial regalia, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T14:01:30-08:00","id":1190421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1189434-begotten-of-the-past?p=1190419#post1190419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe. Also Horrors resembling ghosts of old things - dressed in imperial regalia, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, that reminds me. East Asian lore on ghosts usually say that people who were noble, royal, etc in life become stronger ghosts, their metaphysical weight carrying on beyond death. Ghosts of the empire would make great Horrors in that regard (and likely have Kinship with actual ghosts)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T14:07:59-08:00","id":1190424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1189434-begotten-of-the-past?p=1190421#post1190421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooh, that reminds me. East Asian lore on ghosts usually say that people who were noble, royal, etc in life become stronger ghosts, their metaphysical weight carrying on beyond death. Ghosts of the empire would make great Horrors in that regard (and likely have Kinship with actual ghosts)</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be cool. How's this for an image to go with that:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://i228.photobucket.com/albums/ee138/qwillion/KaidanPromotionalImage.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T14:12:04-08:00","id":1190428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1189434-begotten-of-the-past?p=1190418#post1190418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So something like an undesired Merger taking place? Or more of a &quot;I had Amnesia and in the meantime the inner Monster took over and destroyed everything&quot; kinda deal?<br /> Kinda have to think of it like a Countdown: &quot;Bad news, boy. You got x days, if the conditions are not met, your Horror drives itself into your body and everything that you are or were as a human being disappears to make room for a Gojira running amok. What are the conditions? Pff, fuck if I know.&quot;<br /> Plus maybe losing access to some basic Beast abilities like the instant-positive impression. After all, Kaiju duke it out and except for some team ups are more of a free-for-all-mindset.</div> </div> </div> </div>More on &quot;undesired Merger while still aware until it's too late&quot; kind of things, but the rest is pretty much how I'd do it. Unexplained soul illness that shows early symptoms and culminates into a huge mess. Perhaps spicing it up a bit with bonus on Atavism rolls and Physical Attributes but a load of malus, limitations, loss of not-rampage related powers and Conditions when it's in its advanced state.<br /> <br /> And nobody knows a thing about it. Is it natural? We made it? Humans made it? Does &quot;natural&quot; even have a meaning with us? Monster Mom is ok with this?<br /> <br /> That kind of stuff","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T14:14:07-08:00","id":1190431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1189434-begotten-of-the-past?p=1190424#post1190424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be cool. How's this for an image to go with that:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://i228.photobucket.com/albums/ee138/qwillion/KaidanPromotionalImage.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Yikes. Scary enough for me! (Eshmaki Nemesis?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T14:21:41-08:00","id":1190434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1189434-begotten-of-the-past?p=1190431#post1190431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yikes. Scary enough for me! (Eshmaki Nemesis?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like one to me, although it could be Ugallu as well, for knowing that known only to the dead. Give it the Untouchable, In The Blink of An Eye and What Walks Between fan-Atavisms, along with possibly From The Shadows and Needs Must and you've got something scary. Add in a Nightmare or two like Behold! My True Form and you've got a living ghost story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T15:35:51-08:00","id":1190463,"title":"","content":"I'm glad to see my silly little idea is inspiring a lot of discussion and ideas! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyways, sequel era:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Transformative Heroes (Post-Occupied Japan, 1954-1989)</b></u><br /> <br /> As the years went by, the horrors of WWII and the Occupation that came before it fell into disappearing memory. Moreso when Japan began to prosper under the new economy, becoming the first modern industrialized nation. And with the newest generation of Japanese citizens, the stories from their parents and grandparents about the horrors of the war and the bombs...were just that, stories. And unlikely to be something that would ever happen again. With this newfound prosperity and eye to the future, many people aware of the horrors lurking in the Chronicles of Darkness felt they needed to be dealt with. So when the population of Beasts reached their critical mass, it was only natural that a new wave of Heroes would rise. Either lone Heroes that would fight Begotten one-on-one <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_PzGiDhtfbk\" target=\"_blank\">as so-called &quot;ultramen&quot;</a>. To full <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gbuEg2v9Arg\" target=\"_blank\">Sentais of Heroes</a> (ranging from as small as 3 member groups to as large as 5 members) that would band together to ambush one unlucky Beast or go head-on with full Broods. Attacked from all sides, for the Japanese Beasts it was as if the war had returned for them. But being backed into a corner, that's when any animal can be at their most ferocious. For the Begotten, this is no different, and they sure as hell aren't going to let the newest generation of Heroes have their way.<br /> <br /> (also, Deviant crossover)<br /> <br /> Sometimes though, the heroes that fight the Begotten aren't just limited to those that were touched by the Primordial Dream. Others, particularly large organizations and businesses, saw the Begotten as a threat to their own interests. Deciding not to wait for the Dream to drop a Hero that was aligned with the group's goals and priorities, these Conspiracies decided to build their own heroes. Remade heroes built specifically to find, capture, and kill Beasts, with unwavering loyalty expected from the Conspiracy (either through indoctrination, blackmailing, or torture). Whatever it took, even if it meant kidnapping ordinary and unsuspecting Japanese citizens. Of course, sometimes the Remade break free from bondage to their conspiracies. These Renegades, knowing they can't go back to their old lives, and keenly aware that the horrors of the Chronicles of Darkness isn't something they can turn away from. They either choose to continue to fight Beasts per their original directives, take the fight to their former &quot;masters&quot; (and the Loyalists sent out to re-capture them), or directly aid the Begotten in their conflict against Heroes...or a mixture of all three. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V1PA3Arxevs\" target=\"_blank\">Either way, only they can decide the direction of the ride of their new life.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T15:48:12-08:00","id":1190466,"title":"","content":"Yeah, someone needs to drill in to the Japanese of that era that the horrors of the war aren\u2019t mere stories. Especially when they were the ones inflicting it a few decades ago. No amount of atomic bomb victims can reverse that. And Beasts are perfect instruments of fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T19:39:50-08:00","id":1190536,"title":"","content":"I rised cost of <b>Kaiju </b>Merit to 4 dots. And I moved <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines\">'My Beast' discussion ( with expending to other gamelines )</a> to general CoD forum.<br /> <br /> As to 'Kaiju phenomena as invading infection' problem would be with 'Masquerade' consensus of CoD universe. If humans would turn on to themselves into <i>physical </i>30 meters tall monsters destroying skycrappers- <i>all </i>local military would shoot to that thing. We would have - literally - Kaiju movie in the making in 'reality' of game universe. BUT the differance is that movies do not show consequaces of destroyed half of Tokyo - all those years to rebuild, killed humans, etc. I think that using <i>Looming Presence</i> 'you can show your gigantic monster to some people' and having VERY large Health bar is enough to not break immersion. And still have few Kaiju fights in chronicle - without altering whole of modern Japan history. You still can make Kaiju phenomena more like Condition than Merit - just do not make it into physical Merger of this beast, for gods ( and Japan ) sake!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T20:48:16-08:00","id":1190549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1189434-begotten-of-the-past?p=1190405#post1190405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were to do a post WW2 Japan Era that plays with Kaiju (great idea, by the way) I'd personally explore that element another way. Got no issue with giant Horrors as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4418_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4418\" data-vbnamecard=\"4418\">tasti man LH</a> proposed them, it mirrors the fears of the age and it's absolutely fitting both in an in-setting and meta way, but if I decide to also have more physical Kaiju with a direct mechanical impact, I'd treat them as a condition rather than a Merit. Not a desiderable one, mind you: your Horror grows and pushes from the ephemeral into the material making you lose control of your body and mind. Can it be reversed and fought back? Why is it happening to some Begotten while others seem immune? Who knows, but when a Beast succumbs to it rampage and destruction ensue.<br /> <br /> It shifts it from being a boon into a panic-inducing curse, but plays well with the themes of Beast and the Era. Might even try to make it fit into the current state of Tokyo according to the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say go with both.<br /> <br /> Have it either be new Begotten that have Horrors that are the classic over-sized kaiju, and also have existing Begotten that were active and still alive after the bombs fell take the condition that affects them negatively. We have both the kaiju that impose their fear and destruction that do it with controlled purpose, and also have the ones that are rampaging and out of control. Works for everyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Side note: post WW2 Japan was not just Kaiju movies and there's plenty more to explore, but this reminds me about vague idea I had was about a Era related to classic monster movies. Universal Monsters, sci-fi from the fifties and movies like Blob or The Beast From 20.000 Fathoms. It's a little silly, self-aware and not as dramatic as others, but it's also about a time were the whole Family found a place in medias and common imaginary. But yes, it would require some work and focus in order to function properly. </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah: in of itself, the kaiju and the fears of Japan that powered them are essentially a microcosm on the global anxiety and fears brought on by the Cold War. Where the classic sci-fi B-movies of the time period being representative of them: mutated monster being, of course, nuclear radiation, but also alien invaders being the fear of &quot;da COMMIES&quot; coming in to invade Western countries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T09:45:40-08:00","id":1192296,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4418_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4418\" data-vbnamecard=\"4418\">tasti man LH</a> Sci-Fi and Horror B movies would be a cool setting, though. Due to some Supernatural episodes, I've always wanted a &quot;Monsters of Hollywood&quot; Era set in the 50-80's, but that title/concept is currently probably not the best/most sensitive, given the semi-recent developments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T11:48:18-08:00","id":1192690,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Into the Icy Wastes</b></u><br /> Antarctica - mysterious, mythical, unexplored. A taunting white mark on an otherwise 'explored' world. The last domain of nature resisting human ingenuity, denying them mastery over Earth.<br /> &quot;Well, no more!&quot; said several people, and set out to right this wrong.<br /> They failed for decades, until Amundsen's exploration in 1911 finally succeeded.<br /> What many didn't know: Amundsen wasn't the first by far, and what happened to Scott's expedition wasn't just bad weather. The reports had been modified, and much of their actual discoveries swept under the rug, like the enourmous mountainside and the supposed cubic shapes upon it they discovered. Later expeditions occasionally stumbled upon similar things, too, and quickly succumbed to similar fates. Sometimes it was a mountainside, other times a lake, then again a villade or city.<br /> The survivors of the latest tragedy, a geography professor and a student, prove tight-lipped. Mostly due to insanity in the latter case. However, in certain circles, rumours of strange landscapes, obviously crafted artifacts in a place supposedly uninhabited by humans, of Those Who Came Before, of ruins of a civilisation and a supreme terror abound. Whatever it was, it had to have left a wealth of Chambers of unheard qualities.<br /> Some Begotten feel inexplicably drawn to this place, somehow aware that there are occult mysteries waiting for them. But who was calling them?<br /> Was it the Dark Mother? Was it one of her Young, her first-born? An Apex? THE Apex? Someone, or something, else entirely?<br /> But most importantly: was it worth the risk? Only one way to find out...<br /> <br /> - Obviously, Beasts with Extreme Cold have an advantage on such an enterprise, right?.... <i>right</i>? Imagine their surprise when they suffer from the cold to a degree they couldn't even imagine. Just what on Earth could cause something like that? (Mechanically, Beasts with Extreme Cold suffer double the normal penalties, although they take damage as usual.)<br /> <br /> - The freezing cold is not the only problem. Something about the place is wacky, and time seems to work differently. Some Awakened talk about Time Scars and similar things, but that didn't mean much to the Begotten. They'd rather learn how to <i>leave this eternal noon</i>. (Others are more interested in how they can make this effect part of their Lair...)<br /> <br /> - A Beast returned from an expedition to the South Pole, but it might just as well have been a new person. Not only are they far more powerful, and have Nightmares at their disposal that seem almost alien, they have become far more knowledgeable than they had any right to, easily remembering details about a time before they were alive and capable of occult rites no one ever heard of. Some Elder Kindred and even a Mummy came to disprove them as a fraud, only to find that they were 100% right on everything. However, when asked how this came to pass, they drew a blank: they couldn't remember anything after setting foot on the continent other than a deep feeling of fear. Then, they simply vanished, leaving just a map behind. A map to mountains of madness.<br /> <br /> - A Pack of Werewolves approached the Brood for help, calling in an old but huge debt. Somehow, it has become their task to take down a very powerful Spirit, or non-spirit. It lacked something essential is all the Brood could take away from the frentic talking. To do so, however, they had to enter a cavesystem in Antarctica. Not only would this put a significant dent in the two groups' ressources, there was no guarantee they'd even reach the target alive.<br /> <br /> - When Scott died, the Primordial Dream was shook with such violence that every Beast and Hero across the planet felt it. Something woke up, and it was <i>hungry</i>.<br /> <br /> - An Unchained travelled all through the U.S. and Europe, gathering everyone and everything supernatural willing to listen to him to go to the South Pole. He was able to convince more than one Ring, a few Packs and Broods, a Krewe, some Cabals, some Kindred, even an entire Freehold. This wasn't an expedition, however. It was an army. And none of them expected to come back. Would the Demon be able to convince the players, too? Just what could be this threatening?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T15:52:10-08:00","id":1192828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1189434-begotten-of-the-past?p=1192296#post1192296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4418_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4418\" data-vbnamecard=\"4418\">tasti man LH</a> Sci-Fi and Horror B movies would be a cool setting, though. Due to some Supernatural episodes, I've always wanted a &quot;Monsters of Hollywood&quot; Era set in the 50-80's, but that title/concept is currently probably not the best/most sensitive, given the semi-recent developments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, one of the other ideas stewing in the back of my mind is one big Golden Age of Hollywood crossover Dark Era. Where all of the gamelines would have some representation on the various events happening in and around Hollywood: Kindred pulling the strings of studio execs and famous stars to fill their own pockets, packs of Uratha who assign territory based around the Hisil around the movie studios and on policing the different type of spirits being fostered by the studios, and where for the Awakened, the so-called wizards of cinema are actual wizards. I've already started a bit with my Toontown freehold and courts for changeling.<br /> <br /> SPEAKING OF:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Red Horrors (Hollywood/Los Angeles, 1947-1953)</b></u><br /> <br /> The United States was in an uproar. With President Truman's Executive Order 9835 and requiring all federal civil service employees to be screened for &quot;loyalty&quot;, the beginning of the Cold War in America started in flames as US citizens were suspected left and right for being disloyal to the US of A. With Senator Joseph McCarthy leading the way starting in 1950. No one knows who to trust, who might be a loyal patriot, or who might be a Communist spy. Even more complicated when the political affiliations from the past, back during a time when the US considered the USSR an ally, came back to bite them in unexpected ways.<br /> <br /> A flashpoint for all of this is in Tinsel Town itself, Hollywood. Many of the film industry's prominent screenwriters, directors, and other industry professionals had ties to the Communist Party. The Hollywood Ten leading the way against House of Un-American Activities Committee, declaring how the whole thing was an affront to the Constitution and all the ideals that made America the Land of the Free. Either way, this drove a rift through Hollywood in the people who worked for the silver screen: whether to remain loyal to their colleagues and their art or to remain loyal to the country they lived in. Rifts that, even after<br /> <br /> For Beasts, it's a double-edged sword. On the one hand, the anxiety gripping the country provides a bountiful feast. It doesn't take much to convince a neighbor that their co-worker, their child's teacher, their spouse might be a Communist sympathizer. They don't even have to do the work themselves: they can just convince someone else to do the witch hunts for them. No Begotten during this time went hungry, since they could not go one step without finding a potential source to ease their Satiety. On the other hand, this atmosphere of paranoia could easily be used against them. Any Hero could also use this environment to flush out their mark. And that it was easy to drag out a Beast and brand them a Communist sympathizer. And any unfortunate &quot;accidents&quot; with the accused Begotten before they arrived to court could be brushed aside as some overzealous patriotism. Tricky for Beasts protecting their broodmates, especially when the Hero is drawing in so many unaware civilians who are unfamiliar with the older conflicts from the Primordial Dream, and can't easily justify slaughtering their attackers. After all, if you aren't guilty, why are you resisting so much?<br /> <br /> For the many other creatures of the Chronicles of Darkness, things are no less fun for them: Lancea et Sanctum elders using their political influence to quash Carthian upstarts, the Created finding Hollywood and LA to be uninhabitable since even the most minor bit of Disquiet causes a chain reaction to invoke mobs in record time, and Unchained's Covers risk of compromise nearly every day and being unsure of who the enemy is or if it even is a God Machine plot or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T15:18:36-07:00","id":1200236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1189434-begotten-of-the-past?p=1192690#post1192690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Into the Icy Wastes</b></u><br /> Antarctica - mysterious, mythical, unexplored. A taunting white mark on an otherwise 'explored' world. The last domain of nature resisting human ingenuity, denying them mastery over Earth.<br /> &quot;Well, no more!&quot; said several people, and set out to right this wrong.<br /> They failed for decades, until Amundsen's exploration in 1911 finally succeeded.<br /> What many didn't know: Amundsen wasn't the first by far, and what happened to Scott's expedition wasn't just bad weather. The reports had been modified, and much of their actual discoveries swept under the rug, like the enourmous mountainside and the supposed cubic shapes upon it they discovered. Later expeditions occasionally stumbled upon similar things, too, and quickly succumbed to similar fates. Sometimes it was a mountainside, other times a lake, then again a villade or city.<br /> The survivors of the latest tragedy, a geography professor and a student, prove tight-lipped. Mostly due to insanity in the latter case. However, in certain circles, rumours of strange landscapes, obviously crafted artifacts in a place supposedly uninhabited by humans, of Those Who Came Before, of ruins of a civilisation and a supreme terror abound. Whatever it was, it had to have left a wealth of Chambers of unheard qualities.<br /> Some Begotten feel inexplicably drawn to this place, somehow aware that there are occult mysteries waiting for them. But who was calling them?<br /> Was it the Dark Mother? Was it one of her Young, her first-born? An Apex? THE Apex? Someone, or something, else entirely?<br /> But most importantly: was it worth the risk? Only one way to find out...</div> </div> </div> </div><b>There is new TV series about very much the same idea - <i>The Terror</i>!</b> In 1845 British Navy ship is exploring Arctic to find <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northwest_Passage\" target=\"_blank\">Northwest Passage</a>. On their way they start to have nightmares. And people are found dead. SOMETHING is in the ice around them... Directed by Ridley Scott! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l328p5sSEmc\" data-code=\"l328p5sSEmc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/l328p5sSEmc/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T01:45:33-07:00","id":1200739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1189434-begotten-of-the-past?p=1200236#post1200236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>There is new TV series about very much the same idea - <i>The Terror</i>!</b> In 1845 British Navy ship is exploring Arctic to find <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northwest_Passage&amp;quot;]Northwest</a> Passage[/URL]. On their way they start to have nightmares. And people are found dead. SOMETHING is in the ice around them... Directed by Ridley Scott! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l328p5sSEmc\" data-code=\"l328p5sSEmc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/l328p5sSEmc/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, cool! Thanks for letting me know, looks interesting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T02:52:38-07:00","id":1200745,"title":"","content":"The \u2018discovery\u2019 of America or Australia","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T05:36:15-07:00","id":1200769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1189434-begotten-of-the-past?p=1200745#post1200745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The \u2018discovery\u2019 of America or Australia</div> </div> </div> </div>What sort of unique issues would Beasts experience at those times? More cultural clashes between colonist and native Beasts? What else could you see happening? Some sort of Primordial Dream weirdness is always nice.<br /> <br /> Also, these two times are very far apart. <br /> <br /> How about instead pulling it back to the actual first time people stepped onto those continents. If Horrors are Goetia from the Anima Mundi filtered through human fears, what occurs when humans and all their primal fears encounter a new continent's dreams for the first time?<br /> <br /> First hook for me is a relative outbreak of Insatiables. BPG places their pseudo-horrors as Goetia that entered a host before they matured from contact with the Primordial Dream. With humans new to the continent, the Primordial Dream is thin there and more entities break through without maturing.<br /> <br /> Second hook is the possibility that the Primordial Dream may have already existed in the nightmares of animals and plants, before it got overtaken by humanity's more vivid dreams. Perhaps your group has to deal with strange creatures that steal valuables in the night, or seem to hunt for sport, or otherwise act outside what your knowledge of animals says they should. Are these creatures of a pre-human dream Kin? Enemies like Demons and the Insatiable, or both?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T07:06:22-07:00","id":1200790,"title":"","content":"Animal beasts sounds amazing... pre-human whatever is always sure to get me hyped. Please continue your line of thought! :-D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T08:13:32-07:00","id":1200809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1189434-begotten-of-the-past?p=1200790#post1200790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Animal beasts sounds amazing... pre-human whatever is always sure to get me hyped. Please continue your line of thought! :-D</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> my dude, I got nothing. Rest is up to y'all","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}